Hi KVM/ARM community!

I'm the CEO at Packet and we offer on-demand ARM and intel hardware out 
of 4 global locations (NYC, California, Amsterdam and Tokyo).  We'd like 
to encourage great compatibility for KVM on 64 bit ARM architecture and 
would like to provide free hardware to the KVM community.  We are 
already doing this for people like Docker, MongoDB, NixOS, CentOS, 
FreeBSD, Kubernetes, etc

You can view details on the hardware here: 
https://www.packet.net/bare-metal/servers/type-2a/

You can use standard devops tools (e.g. ansible, terraform, libcloud) 
and cloud-init to bootstrap these.  It could be good for long term or 
on-demand testing.

Please let me know if anybody is interested so we can get you setup.

thanks!
-- 
